  "implemented_behavior": "Directed graph and intervention/counterfactual fidelity in declared acyclic linear structural causal models.",
  "bounded_contract": "Reference model: each node has id,intercept,noise,parents {node,coefficient}. All nodes/edges unique, acyclic, bounded, with nonzero edge coefficients. Queries specify positive weight, interventions,target,inference_kind.\nSolve in topological order. A do intervention replaces the intervened node equation, not its exogenous ancestors. Fixed noise is retained for explicitly labeled counterfactual_fixed_noise queries. Candidate edges and numeric query answers are checked independently against trusted model.\nTrue edges contribute weight1; queries have declared weights. Missing/reversed edges lose credit; unsupported extra edges veto PASS. Association cannot be relabeled as intervention/counterfactual; correct numbers with wrong inference_kind fail.",
  "bounds_and_open_scope": "No empirical identification, causal discovery, proof of real-world causal validity, stochastic uncertainty estimation or universal counterfactual reasoning. Model assumptions and noise are supplied and require independent validation.",
